STATE
The application will use React's `useState` and `useEffect` hooks to manage data, user interactions, API requests, and local storage.

### State Tree

```text
THE BEAUTY EDIT
│
└── App.jsx
    │
    ├── products
    │   └── Stores products fetched from the DummyJSON API
    │
    ├── wishlist
    │   └── Stores products saved by the user
    │       └── Persisted in localStorage
    │
    ├── loading
    │   └── Tracks whether the API is loading
    │
    ├── error
    │   └── Stores API error messages
    │
    ├── searchTerm
    │   └── Stores the user's product search input
    │
    ├── selectedCategory
    │   └── Stores the currently selected product category
    │
    ├── editingId
    │   └── Tracks which wishlist product is being edited
    │
    └── formData
        └── Stores the values entered into the add/edit product form
```

### Where Each State Lives

| State | Location | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `products` | App.jsx | Stores products fetched from the API |
| `wishlist` | App.jsx | Stores the user's saved products |
| `loading` | App.jsx | Tracks API loading status |
| `error` | App.jsx | Handles API errors |
| `searchTerm` | App.jsx | Stores the search input |
| `selectedCategory` | App.jsx | Stores the selected category filter |
| `editingId` | App.jsx | Identifies the product being edited |
| `formData` | AddProductForm / EditProductForm | Stores form input values |

### State Persistence

The wishlist will be saved in the browser's `localStorage` so that user-created data remains available after refreshing or reopening the application.

- `useState` will manage the wishlist and other application states.
- `useEffect` will fetch products from the API when the application loads.
- Another `useEffect` will update `localStorage` whenever the wishlist changes.

### State Sharing Through Props

The main application state will live in `App.jsx` and be passed down to child components through props.

For example:
- `products` will be passed to `BrowseSection` and `ProductList`.
- `wishlist` will be passed to `WishlistSection` and `WishlistList`.
- Functions for adding, editing, and deleting wishlist items will be passed to the relevant child components.
- Search and category values will be passed to the browsing components.

